# Documentation policy

- ALL research, architecture, and knowledge artifacts for this repo → `docs/src/architecture/` (NOT IDE knowledge bases)
- In `docs/src/`, only fenced blocks whose language tag is `vox` are passed through the Vox compiler for doctest. Write inline `vox` blocks that compile; do not add new `{{#include}}` directives. Use `// vox:skip` plus a reason only when a snippet is intentionally non-normative (an out-of-file excerpt, pseudo-code, or invalid on purpose). Other language tags (`tsx`, `rust`, …) are not parsed as Vox
- Do NOT edit derived ignore files (`.cursorignore`, `.aiignore`, `.aiexclude`) — edit `.voxignore` and run `vox ci sync-ignore-files`
- Do NOT read or modify `docs/src/archive/` for new feature work
- New doc pages need the frontmatter and KB facets in `docs/src/contributors/documentation-governance.md` (`title`, `description`, `category`, `status`, `topic`, `domain`, `authorship`, plus a `kb:summary` block). Never hand-author `last_updated`: the lint rejects it, and the date comes from Git history
